Let  $O$  be the circumcentre of  $\displaystyle \triangle ADF$ . Then  $\angle DOF = 2A$ . On the other hand,  $\angle DEB = 180^{\circ} - 2B$  and  $\angle FEC = 180^{\circ} - 2C$ , therefore  $\angle DEF = 180^{\circ} - 2A$ .

Thus,  $D,O,F,E$  are concyclic.  $OD = OF$  implies that  $O$  is the midpoint of the arc  $DF$ , and hence  $EO$  bisects  $\angle DEF$ .  $\square$

