Nice quick exercise :D $\color{black}\rule{25cm}{1pt}$ Let  $M$  be the intersection of  $PY$  with  $AX$ .

Since we have that  $\angle YPQ=\angle YCQ=\angle YCA=\angle YXA$  we have that  $AX$  is tangent to the circumcircle of  $PXY$ .
But also notice that we have that  $\angle YAX = \angle YCB = \angle YPA$ , thus we have that  $AX$  is tangent to the circumcircle of  $PYA$ .

Thus by power of a point we have that  $MX ^2=MY.MP=MA^2$ .
This implies that  $MX=MA$ .

