Let us substitute  $b = 51 - a - c$  into the second equation to obtain: $ac(51 - a - c) = 4000$ ;

or  $51ac - a^2c - ac^2 = 4000$ ;

or  $ac^2 + (a^2 - 51a)c + 4000$ ;

or  $c = \frac{(51a - a^2) \pm \sqrt{(a^2 - 51a)^2 - 16000a}}{2a} \ge 25$ ;

or  $\pm \sqrt{(a^2 - 51a)^2 - 16000a}{2a} \ge a^2 - a$ ;

or  $(a^2 - 51a)^2 - 16000a \ge a^4 - 2a^3 + a^2$ ;

or  $0 \ge 100a^3 - 2600a^2 + 16000a$ ;

or  $0 \ge a^3 - 26a^2 + 160a$ ;

or  $0 \ge a(a - 10)(a - 16)$ ;

or  $a \in (-\infty, 0] \cup [10, 16]$   (NOTE:  $0 < a \le 10$ );

or **<span style="color:#f00">a = 10</span>**.

This result leaves us  $b + c = 41$  and  $bc = 400$ , which is solved according to: $c(41 - c) = 400$ ;

or  $0 = c^2 - 41c + 400 = (c - 16)(c - 25)$ ;

or  $c = 16, 25$   (NOTE:  $c \ge 25$ );

or ***<span style="color:#f00">c = 25</span>*** and **<span style="color:#f00">b =  16</span>**.

Thus, the only solution is  $\fbox{(a, b, c) = (10, 16, 25)}$ .

