Since  $AB=AC$ , it follows that  $BF=4$  as well, and that  $AE=AF$ . Let  $AE=AF=x$ ,  $X$  be the foot of the perpendicular from  $A$  to  $EF$ , and  $y$  be the length of  $EF$ . 

Since  $EF\parallel BC$ , then  $\triangle AFE\sim\triangle ABC$ . Then, \[\frac{x}{x+4}=\frac{y}{12}.\] The similarity also tells us that  $\angle AEF=\angle DCE$ . Thus,  $\triangle AXE\sim\triangle DEC$  by AA similarity. So \[\frac{x}{6}=\frac{y}{8}.\]

From our two proportions, we have \begin{align}12x&=xy+4y 8x&=6y.\end{align} Then  $x=\frac{3y}{4}$  and then \[9y=\frac{3y^2}{4}+4y\implies y=\frac{20}{3}.\] Thus,  $EF=\boxed{\frac{20}{3}}$ .

